    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-324397",
      "knowledge_point_id": "387e57ad-6f80-5b90-8adf-7bf05618b532",
      "knowledge_point": "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Secant with Non-Special Angles",
      "problem": "Find, **in ascending order and rounded to one decimal place**, the two solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=-2.3$ for $0\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$\nand $x=$ \n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ Therefore the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=-\\frac{1}{2.3}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal value of $x,$ rounded to three decimal places:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=arccos\\,(-\\frac{1}{2.3})≈{115.771}^{∘}\n$$\n\nOur first solution lies in the $2$nd quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}≈{180}^{∘}-{115.771}^{∘}≈{64.229}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the $3$rd quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}≈{64.229}^{∘}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977622/assets/974fad6534267df035b759df9064ed7dfaff80cb299c41744e8888f248ed1eee.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{∘}+{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ≈{180}^{∘}+{64.229}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈{244.229}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, in ascending order and rounded to one decimal place, the solutions are $x=115.8\\,{\\,}^{∘}$ and $x=244.2\\,{\\,}^{∘}.$",
