    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-30468",
      "knowledge_point_id": "387e57ad-6f80-5b90-8adf-7bf05618b532",
      "knowledge_point": "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Secant with Non-Special Angles",
      "problem": "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $4(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-4)=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘},$ what is the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to the nearest integer?",
      "worked_solution": "We first simplify the given equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-4) & =3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x \\\\ 4\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-16 & =3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x \\\\ \\operatorname{sec}⁡x & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},$ therefore the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\frac{1}{16}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{16})=86.416\\,678{…}^{∘}≈{86.417}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${86.417}^{∘}$ lies inside the required domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={86.417}^{∘}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the first quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={86.417}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the fourth quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={86.417}^{∘}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977622/assets/15e99d348206191535a2b6fb9d85893e666abd16f5f9fc61fdf4e19424e2fde9.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $4$th quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={360}^{∘}-{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={360}^{∘}-{86.417}^{∘} \\\\  & ={273.583}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=86.417\\cdot 273.583≈23\\,642,\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.",
