      "knowledge_point_id": "28062dbf-815b-5221-ae86-1050e106c5ea",
      "knowledge_point": "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Secant Under a Modified Domain",
      "problem": "Find the two solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}$ for $-{180}^{∘}\\le x<{180}^{∘}.$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$\nand $x=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{3}})={30}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince ${30}^{∘}$ lies inside the required domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={30}^{∘}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the first quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={30}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the fourth quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={30}^{∘}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977622/assets/3f3f1422eca9190a5e0827da456315ba88b074f0bf5e9aab1bb325d131bf1984.png)\n\nAnother solution $X$ lies in the $4$th quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={360}^{∘}-{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={360}^{∘}-{30}^{∘} \\\\  & ={330}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, this value is not in the required domain. To get the second solution ${x}_{2}$ that's within the given domain, we subtract ${360}^{∘}:$\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}={330}^{∘}-{360}^{∘}=-{30}^{∘}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-30\\,{\\,}^{∘}$ and $x=30\\,{\\,}^{∘}.$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "-30"
            }
